    "article_summary": "This article describes a visible-light-driven, dual photoredox/nickel-catalyzed carboxylation of (hetero)aryl and vinyl bromides using sodium formate as a CO2 source. A key finding is the essential role of phenyl triflimide (PhN(SO2CF3)2) as a catalytic sulfonylating agent/HAT catalyst that activates formate, enabling the reaction to proceed under mild conditions for electron-rich and neutral substrates that were previously challenging.",
